  * The idea here is that some structures may not specify a name which should then result in a different name being generated.
  * For example, if you create a structure like this:
    
      ```js
      const Struct = require('structured-types');
      
      new Struct({
        value: Number
      });
      ```
  
    Then even though the type has no properties, its name will still be 'Number' because it cannot determine what the value would look like e.g. 'NumbersWithNanAndInf'.
  * If the structure does not have one set it will just use the default name: 'Struct'
 *
 * @param {Structure} struc The structure to get the name for
 * @returns {string} The name
